<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply off $11.1 bln in Sept 23 wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply off $11.1 bln in Sept 23 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply fell $11.1 billion in the September 23 week to $3,759.6 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $8.7 billion to $4,779.9 billion. M-1 fell $3.5 billion to $1,088.0 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,765.0 billion versus $3,764.3 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
